<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11297" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cor-rīvo</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">conr-</span></b> ), āvi, ātum,
		1, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. a.,
				to conduct streams of water together, to draw together into one
				stream</i> (post-Aug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">venas aquarum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Q. N. 3, 19, 4</span></i>
			; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aquam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig.
					39, 3, 3</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Plin. 31, 4, 30, § 53</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">liquorem salis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 6,
					14, 17, § 43</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tiberim piscinis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 3,
					5, 9, § 53</span></i>
			; with <i>in aliquid</i>, <i><span class="en">id. 6, 16,
				18, § 47</span></i>.</div>
